{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For you shall come.</b> And it does not say תָּבִיא ('you shall bring'), for HaShem is the one who brings them, as He said above: ״HaShem your Elohim — He it is who crosses… He it is who will destroy״ — except that he [Joshua] will come at their head. And although the Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 8a) regarding the verse that He said at the end of the parashah (Deuteronomy 31:23) ״כִּי אַתָּה תָּבִיא״ — that the Holy One, blessed be He, said one thing for the generation — since the sense of תָּבוֹא ('you shall come') can also bear [the meaning that] others are with him, therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to make His words explicit. And in any event Moses' intention was to indicate that HaShem is the one who brings [them]. You thus find that he said ״תָּבוֹא״ to fix the deed in HaShem, for He is the one who brings, and he said ״תָּבִיא״ to exclude anyone else from the human side."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:44.023654153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}